    "chunk_text": "6. The names of persons whom the Medal is conferred upon, shall be published in the respective Service Ordersand a register of all such recipients shall be maintained under the direction of the respective Service Commander.\n\n9. Every Soldier, Seaman, Airman and Policemen who has been discharged from the Army, Navy and Air Forcewith disgrace or with ignominy, shall forfeit the Medal unless His Excellency the President shall direct otherwise.\n\n13. In an event where a Medal is lost, and if it is desirous to replace it, such a loss should be reported to the Police.A declaration testified by a Justice of the Peace stating the circumstances under which the loss occurred should be submit-ted along with a copy of the complaint made to the Police. This declaration shall be forwarded to the Commanding Officerwho will forward it to the respective Service Commander through the usual channel of communication. The Medal losttherewith will be replaced on payment if the explanation as to the loss is considered satisfactory.\n\n14. In those Regulations -\n\n(a)\"Services\" means-The Sri Lanka Army,The Sri Lanka Navy,The Sri Lanka Air Force,\n\n(b)\"Police\" meansThe Sri Lanka Police.\n\n(c)\"Service Commanders\" means-The Commander of the Army,The Commander of the Navy,The Commander of the Air Force,\n\n(d)\"Inspector General\" means-The Inspector General of Police.\n\n(e)\"Military Personnel\" means-Army, Navy and Air Force personnel\n\n(f)\"Member of Police\" means-Police Personnel\n\n(g)\"Member of the Civil Staff\" means-Civilians working in the Army,Navy, Air Force and Police.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'10'21PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 21.10.20194A\n\n(h)\"Army\" means-The Sri Lanka Army\n\n(i)\"Navy\" means-The Sri Lanka Navy\n\n(j)\"Air Force\" means-The Sri Lanka Air Force\n\n(k)\"Police\" means-The Sri Lanka Police\n\n11 - 661/1\n\nAMENDMENT\n\nSERVICE MEDAL\n\nOrders"
