    "chunk_text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'08'27PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 27.08.20191A\n\nwxl 2146$36 - 2019 Tlaf;dan\u00be ui 25 jeks isl=rdod - 2019'10'25No. 2146/36 - FRIDAY OCTOBER 25, 2019\n\n(Published by Authority)PART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\nAppointments & C., by the President\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A - G 31332\u2014 377(10/2019)\n\nNo. 750/1 of 2019\n\nP. S. No. : PS/CSA/00/9/1/4/1\n\nIT is hereby notified that His Excellency the President has been pleased to appoint the following persons as Commissionersof the Mediation Boards Commission, with immediate effect, under the Provisions of Section 2(1) of the MediationBoards Act, No. 72 of 1988.\n\n1.Justice Hector Yapa- Retired Judge of the Supreme Court2.Justice Nimal Dissanayake- Retired Judge of the Supreme Court3.Justice Chandradasa Nanayakkara- Retired Judge of the Court of Appeal4.Mr. M. Somasundaram5.Mrs. Faleela Be Jurangpathy\n\nHis Excellency the President has nominated Justice Hector Yapa, retired Supreme Court Judge under the above-mentioned provisions, to be the Chairman of the said Commission.\n\nBy His Excellency\u2019s Command,\n\nUDAYA R. SENEVIRATNE,Secretary to the President.Presidential Secretariat,Colombo 01,October 23, 2019.\n\n11- 798\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
