    "chunk_text": "(3) The Teller shall be responsible for the collection of the user fee at every gate referred to in paragraph (2), in such sum as is specified in Part A of the Schedule to these regulations from every driver using such User Fee National Highways :\n\n(7) The Teller shall at such times as are specified, hand over the day\u2019s collection of the fees to the officer authorized in that behalf by the Authority and obtain a receipt in respect of such amount.\n\n(8) The money so collected as user fee shall be credited to the Fund of the Authority and be used for the purpose of developing and maintaining the User Fee National Highways to which these regulations apply.\n\n(9) For the purpose of these regulations-\n\n\u201cDesignated location\u201d means an authorized access point, where a driver of a vehicle is permitted to enter the User Fee National Highway without obtaining a ticket and includes New Kelani Interchange, Peliyagoda Interchange, Katunayake Interchange, Katunayake (25.8km) and Kerawalapitiya Interchange.\n\n\u201cE- Tag\u201d means an electronic device that is permanently installed on the windscreen or head lamp of the vehicle for the purpose of payment of user fee electronically when passing through an Electronic User Fee Lane.\n\n\u201cTeller\u201d means an officer who is manning the gates at an interchange;\n\n\u201cUser Fee National Highways\u201d includes the Southern User Fee National Highway from Kottawa (0.000 km) to Pinnaduwa (95.275 km), Galle \u2013 Matara User Fee National Highway from Pinnaduwa (95.275km) to Godagama (124.806 km), Godagama \u2013 Kasagala Section of Southern Expressway User Fee National Highway from Godagama (124.806 km) to Kasagala (163.456 km), Colombo \u2013 Katunayake User Fee National Highway from Colombo (0.000km) to Katunayake (25.800km) and Outer Circular User fee National Highway from Kottawa (0.000 km) to Kerawalapitiya (28.867km)"
