    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'14PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.11.20192A\n\nPART I\n\nRegistration of Ayurvedic Hotels\n\n(a)submit an application to the Director-General of the Authority (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cDirector-General\u201d) in a form determined by him ; and\n\n(b)accompanied by such fees specified in the Order made under subsection (5) of section 48 of the TourismAct, No. 38 of 2005 and published in Extraordinary Gazette No. 2071/57 dated May 16, 2018.\n\n5. The Director-General may request for further information or documents to be furnished, including anyclarification that he may consider to be necessary for the purpose of deciding such application.\n\n6. An application found to contain false, misleading or incorrect information or particulars shall be rejected.\n\n7. Where the Director-General satisfies that the applicant possess the requirements mentioned herein, the Director-General shall register such applicant as registered proprietor of such Ayurvedic Hotel and, issue a Certificate of registrationto such registered proprietor.\n\n8. Upon the registration of such Ayurvedic Hotel, the Authority may issue a Certificate of Standards to theproprietor of such Ayurvedic Hotel containing minimum standards of such enterprise.\n\nPART II\n\nLicensing of Registered Ayurvedic Hotels\n\n9. (1) Every person who desires to carry on a business of an Ayurvedic Hotel registered under these regulationsshall -\n\n(a)submit an application to the Director-General in a form determined by him ; and\n\n(b)accompanied by such fees specified in the Order made under subsection (5) of Section 48 of the TourismAct, No. 38 of 2005 and published in Extraordinary Gazette No. 2071/57 dated May 16, 2018.\n\n(2) Every application under paragraph (I) shall be accompanied by a detailed report setting out the capacity andability of the Ayurvedic Hotel."
  },
