    "chunk_text": "(b)accompanied by such fees specified in the Order made under subsection (5) of Section 48 of the TourismAct, No. 38 of 2005 and published in Extraordinary Gazette No. 2071/57 dated May 16, 2018.\n\n(2) Every application under paragraph (I) shall be accompanied by a detailed report setting out the capacity andability of the Ayurvedic Hotel.\n\n11.(a)The Director-General shall, on being satisfied that the applicant possesses the minimum standardsspecified in the Certificate of Standards for Ayurvedic Hotel issue a license to the proprietor of theAyurvedic Hotel.\n\n(b)The Director-General shall, in writing within a period of one month inform the applicant of his decisionand in a case of a refusal to grant license, he shall state his reasons therefore.\n\n12. The license issued under regulation 11 of these regulations -\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'14PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.11.20193A\n\n(a)may be subject to such terms and conditions as specified in the license, which the Director-Generalmay deem appropriate for securing due compliance with provisions of Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005 orany regulations made thereunder.\n\n(b)shall come into force on the date specified therein ; and\n\n(c)shall unless it is earlier cancelled or revoked by the Director-General, remain in force for a period ofone year from the date specified in the license.\n\nPART III\n\nGeneral\n\n13. The Director-General may refuse to issue a license under regulation 11 where the applicant -\n\n(a)has failed to register the tourist enterprise of the Ayurvedic Hotel or himself as the registered proprietorunder these regulations ; or\n\n(c)has failed to comply with minimum standards specified in the Certificate of Standards issued underthese regulations."
