    "chunk_text": "(a)has failed to register the tourist enterprise of the Ayurvedic Hotel or himself as the registered proprietorunder these regulations ; or\n\n(c)has failed to comply with minimum standards specified in the Certificate of Standards issued underthese regulations.\n\n15. The Director-General may cancel the Certificate of Registration issued under regulation 7 or license issuedunder regulation 11 of these regulations on the ground -\n\n(a)that any provisions of the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005 has been violated ;\n\n(b)that any regulations made under the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005 has been violated ; or\n\n(c)that any condition attached to the Certificate of Registration issued under regulation 7 or license issuedunder regulation 11 has not been complied with.\n\n16. A license issued under regulation 11 of these regulations shall be renewable -\n\n(a)on an application being made on that behalf to the Director-General in a form as may be determined byhim ;\n\n(b)not later than three months before the expiry of the license ; and\n\n(c)be accompanied by such fees as are payable in terms of the order made under subsection (5) of section48 of the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005 published in Gazette No. 2071/57 dated May 16, 2018.\n\n17. Any person aggrieved by a decision of, refusal to issue the Certificate of Registration or refusal of a renewalor a cancellation of a license issued may, within one month of the date of receipt of the written communications informingsuch person of the refusal or the cancellation, as the case may be, submit an appeal to the Tribunal established underSection 51 of the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005.\n\n18. Every registered and licensed proprietor shall ensure the registered Ayurvedic Hotel complies with theminimum requirements as specified in Schedule hereto.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'14PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.11.20194A"
