    "chunk_text": "18. Every registered and licensed proprietor shall ensure the registered Ayurvedic Hotel complies with theminimum requirements as specified in Schedule hereto.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'14PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.11.20194A\n\n20. In these regulations -\n\n\u201cAyurvedic Hotel\u201d means an enterprise which is dedicated to provide indigenous or traditional Ayurvedichealth care services to enhance mental, physical and spiritual wellbeing of the guests.\n\nSchedule\n\n(Section 18)\n\n1.0 Minimum Requirements for Ayurvedic Health Care Hotel\n\n1.1 Location\n\nThe minimum requirements of the particular classified Hotel to be complied with the Tourism (Classificationof Tourist Hotels) regulation No. 1 of 2016 published in the Gazette Extraordinary No. 1963/28 datedApril 20, 2016\n\n1.2 Buildings\n\nThe buildings shall be suitably designed and constructed for provision of Ayurvedic health care services.\n\n1.3 Compound and Garden\n\nThe compound and the garden shall be well laid out and maintained to harmonize with the requirements ofAyurvedic health care services, preferably grown with Ayurvedic herbs.\n\n1.4 Parking\n\nThere shall be dedicated parking space for the guests of the Ayurvedic healh care component.\n\n1.5 Reception/Information\n\nA separate Reception/Information desk shall be made available to receive and provide detailed informationon Ayurvedic health care service to the guests.\n\n1.6 Consultation Rooms and Guest Waiting Rooms\n\n1.6.1 There shall be one or more consultation room/s with adequate space and facilities for physician.\n\n1.6.2 These rooms shall be demarcated, adequately lit and ventilated and shall be well maintained.\n\n1.6.3 Comfortable seating facilities shall be provided for the physicians as well as for guests seekingtreatments."
  },
