    "chunk_size_bytes": 1946,
    "chunk_text": "1.6.2 These rooms shall be demarcated, adequately lit and ventilated and shall be well maintained.\n\n1.6.3 Comfortable seating facilities shall be provided for the physicians as well as for guests seekingtreatments.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'14PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.11.20195A\n\n1.7 Types of Ayurvedic Treatments\n\nThe Ayurvedic Health Care Unit shall provide the following types of Ayurvedic treatments.\n\n1.7.1 Poorva Karma (Sneha an Sweda Karmal, namely (a) Thaila Abyanga and Sheera Abyanga, (b) Shirodhara,(c) Sarwangadhara (d) Pinda and Wasshpa Swedha, (e) Agni and Niranga Swedha.\n\n1.7.2 Pradhana Karma (Pancha Karma) namely (a) Vamana Karma, (b) Viredhana Karma, (c) Nasya Karma,(d) Vasthi Karma, (e) Raktha Mokshana Karma.\n\n1.7.3 Paschath Karma, (a) Patya Ahara Viharana.\n\n1.7.4 Kshudra Karma, namely (a) Gandusha, (b) Kavalangraha and (c) Akshi Tharpana.\n\n1.7.5 Shamana Karma, namely (a) Deepana, (b) Paachana, (c) Athapa and (d) Sevana.\n\n1.8 Treatment Rooms\n\n1.8.1 The treatment rooms shall be located away from the public areas and there shall be adequate privacy inan around the room.\n\n1.8.2 Adequate number of treatment rooms shall be provided in relation to the number of rooms and guestsseeking following therapeutical treatments ; namely (a) massage, (b) steam baths, (d) other treatment,(e) herbal baths, (f) acupuncture (if provided), meditation and yoga and counseling.\n\n1.8.3 There shall be separate treatment rooms for male and female guests.\n\n1.8.4 The following facilities and equipment shall be made available for treatment purpose, namely (a)Examination bed/s, (b) Wooden beds for massage/Shirodhara and (c) Caskets made out of wood(preferably Margosa) for steaming.\n\n1.8.5 Treatment rooms shall have sufficient light and ventilation.\n\n1.8.6 Adequate No. of showers shall be provided."
  },
