    "chunk_text": "1.8.4 The following facilities and equipment shall be made available for treatment purpose, namely (a)Examination bed/s, (b) Wooden beds for massage/Shirodhara and (c) Caskets made out of wood(preferably Margosa) for steaming.\n\n1.8.5 Treatment rooms shall have sufficient light and ventilation.\n\n1.8.6 Adequate No. of showers shall be provided.\n\n1.9 Post - Treatment Relaxation Lounge/Area\n\n1.9.1 There shall be a separate post-treatment relaxation lounge or are for relaxation after treatment.\n\n1.9.2 It shall be well equipped and furnished with relaxing chairs and shall be without any disturbances.\n\n1.10 Pharmacy and Medical preparation room\n\n1.10.1 There shall be a spacious pharmacy for stocking of Ayurvedic supplies and for preparation of medicine.\n\n1.10.2 Preparation of medicine shall be done under the supervision of a qualified Ayurvedic Physician orqualified pharmacist, registered with the Ayurvedic Medical Council.\n\n1.10.3 Suitable racks and storing devices shall be provided for storage of medicinal items and tables, equipmentand utensils shall be provided for mixing and preparation of medicine.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'14PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.11.20196A\n\n1.10.4 The pharmacy shall be fitted with a wash basin with running hot and cold water.\n\n1.10.5 All drugs/medicines shall be prepared according to the accepted standards using permitted utensils.\n\n1.10.6 Manufactured drugs and raw materials shall be stored separately.\n\n1.10.7 Proper and adequate heating and fermentation methods shall be observed.\n\n1.10.8 The Pharmacist shall maintain an inventory of all pharmaceuticals, indicating date of manufacture, dateof expiry, ingredients used and details of suppliers of manufacturers."
