    "chunk_text": "1.10.7 Proper and adequate heating and fermentation methods shall be observed.\n\n1.10.8 The Pharmacist shall maintain an inventory of all pharmaceuticals, indicating date of manufacture, dateof expiry, ingredients used and details of suppliers of manufacturers.\n\n1.11 Herbal Kitchen\n\n1.11.1 There shall be a herbal kitchen with adequate knowledgeable and experienced staff for the preparationof required solid and liquid herbal products, decoctions, pastes and bundles.\n\n1.11.2 Utensils used for the preparation of all Ayurvedic medicine in the Health Care Unit shall have theapproval of the Department of Ayurveda.\n\n1.12 Casual Toilets Units\n\n1.12.1 There shall be separate casual toilet units for males and females.\n\n1.12.2 There shall be separate changing rooms, where necessary.\n\n1.12.3 Each toilet unit shall be provided with water closet (W. C.) units, wash basins, mirrors, towel rails,clothes hooks, clean towels, sanitary bin with paper bags, soap trays, toilet paper with holders, bidetsor hand bidets and hot and cold water.\n\n1.12.4 The fixtures and fittings in the casual toilet units shall be in good working order.\n\n1.12.5 Adequate separate shower shall be available.\n\n1.12.6 The toilet units shall be adequately lit and ventilated and also well maintained.\n\n1.12.7 The floors and walls up to 1.5 m of the toilet shall be of impervious material.\n\n1.13 Staff and Facilities\n\n1.13.1 There shall be at least one Ayurvedic Physician certified by Department Ayurveda/Ayurveda MedicalCouncil as a consultant attached to the Ayurvedic Health Care Unit, preferably with an Assistant Physicianwho shall have a Degree or Diploma from and institute recognized by the Department of Ayurveda. Anytraditional Indigenous Ayurvedic Physician shall have obtained necessary clearance from the Departmentof Ayurveda, based on their proven track records."
