    "chunk_text": "1.13.1 There shall be at least one Ayurvedic Physician certified by Department Ayurveda/Ayurveda MedicalCouncil as a consultant attached to the Ayurvedic Health Care Unit, preferably with an Assistant Physicianwho shall have a Degree or Diploma from and institute recognized by the Department of Ayurveda. Anytraditional Indigenous Ayurvedic Physician shall have obtained necessary clearance from the Departmentof Ayurveda, based on their proven track records.\n\n1.13.3 Attendants, both male and female, with at least six months training and practical experience in Ayurveda,shall be available to treat the male and female patients respectively.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'14PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.11.20197A\n\n1.13.4 The Physician or at least one member of the staff shall be proficient in English or any other relevantforeign language.\n\n1.13.5 Separate and clean toilets with water closet in working order shall be available for the use of the staff.\n\n1.13.6 There shall be separate staff changing rooms for males and females, equipped with necessary furnitureand furnishing.\n\n1.13.7 If staff staying overnight, adequate accommodation shall be available\n\n1.13.8 Staff shall be provided with uniforms appropriate for the Ayurvedic service provided.\n\n1.13.9 There shall be a staff dining room appropriately furnished and equipped.\n\n1.14 General\n\n1.14.1 Emergency medical facilities/arrangement, such as First Aid and hospital transfer, shall be available, ifand when necessary.\n\n1.14.2 Guests\u2019 reports/medical profiles/patient history records that include medicines prescribed, by whomthe medicines were prescribed and the treatments given shall be maintained and shall be able to produceupon request.\n\n1.14.3 The Hotel shall obtain certificate from Department of Ayurveda.\n\n1.14.4 Insurance cover with public liability with minimum of rupees five million shall be obtained."
